{"id": "EUVD-2026-97718", "enisaUuid": "7560668c-c53c-3126-8420-ef2527beb553", "description": "ImageMagick before 7.1.2-32 contains a time-of-check time-of-use symlink race vulnerability that allows attackers to bypass the path security policy when executing a magick script. Attackers can swap a checked path with a symlink during script execution to read files that the security policy is meant to block.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:55:57", "baseScore": 2.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-7q74-r26w-fwcx", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/9e789499e67dbf5c4ee9fe1b72690738c799ec73", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-7.1.2-32-toctou-symlink-race-path-policy-bypass-via-magick-script"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109274", "GHSA-849g-2wm5-pm7c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3a66506e-0f5a-307c-a375-052ae195b328", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-32"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fd6774d8-57ea-36ca-93bc-93f73a88f730", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}